.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ntag424_setup "(1)"
.SH NAME
ntag424_setup \- Register NTAG424 DNA NFC cards in the policy config
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ntag424_setup
\-u \fIuser\fR \-\-uid \fIhex\fR (\-\-issuer\-key \fIhex\fR | \-\-k1 \fIhex\fR \-\-k2 \fIhex\fR | \-\-use\-defaults)
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ntag424_setup
registers an NTAG424 DNA NFC card (typically a Bolt Card deployment)
in the policy configuration file used by
.BR pam_pcsc_cr (8).
The card is assumed to already be deployed with known keys.
.PP
Keys can be provided in three mutually exclusive ways:
explicit per-card keys (\-\-k1/\-\-k2),
per-card issuer key for deterministic derivation (\-\-issuer\-key),
or no per-card keys at all (\-\-use\-defaults, requires a
.B [defaults]
section in the config file).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u " user"
PAM username to associate with this card (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-uid " hex"
7-byte card UID as 14 hex characters (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-issuer\-key " hex"
16-byte issuer key as 32 hex characters.
Stores the issuer key in the card entry; K1/K2 are derived at
authentication time using the Bolt Card deterministic algorithm.
Cannot be combined with \-\-k1/\-\-k2 or \-\-use\-defaults.
.TP
.BI \-\-card\-version " int"
Card version for key derivation (default: 1).
Only meaningful with \-\-issuer\-key.
.TP
.BI \-\-k1 " hex"
SDM decryption key (K1) as 32 hex characters.
Must be used together with \-\-k2.
.TP
.BI \-\-k2 " hex"
CMAC verification key (K2) as 32 hex characters.
Must be used together with \-\-k1.
.TP
.BI \-c " path"
Path to the policy configuration file.
If omitted, defaults to
.BR /etc/ntag424.conf .
The file is created if it does not exist.
Must be owned by root and mode 0600 (contains key material).
.TP
.BI \-\-id " label"
Card section label in the config file.
If omitted, auto-generated as \fBcard-<user>-<uid>\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing card entry with the same ID.
Without this flag, duplicate card IDs cause an error.
.TP
.B \-\-use\-defaults
Do not store per-card key material.
The card's K1/K2 will be derived at authentication time from the
.B [defaults]
section's
.B issuer_key
in the config file.
Cannot be combined with \-\-k1/\-\-k2/\-\-issuer\-key.
Requires that the config file already has a
.B [defaults]
section with an
.B issuer_key.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register a Bolt Card using deterministic key derivation:
.sp
.nf
sudo ntag424_setup \e
    \-u alice \e
    \-\-uid 04996c6a926980 \e
    \-\-issuer\-key 00000000000000000000000000000001 \e
    \-c /etc/ntag424.conf
sudo chmod 600 /etc/ntag424.conf
.fi
.sp
Register a card using global defaults (simplest, requires [defaults] in config):
.sp
.nf
sudo ntag424_setup \e
    \-u alice \e
    \-\-uid 04996c6a926980 \e
    \-\-use\-defaults \e
    \-c /etc/ntag424.conf
sudo chmod 600 /etc/ntag424.conf
.fi
.sp
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/ntag424.conf
Policy configuration file mapping cards to PAM users.
Contains key material (K1/K2 and/or issuer keys) and must be
.BR root:root " mode " 0600 .
.TP
.B /var/lib/ntag424/replay.db
SQLite database for replay counter tracking.
Should be
.BR root:root " mode " 0600 .
